-- title:
--   Residue fields of the Gauss rings of X₁(Mp) and X₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Inside $L((q))$ let $K$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$, i.e. of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios of integral forms of level $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, and let $K'$ be the corresponding field for level $M$, assumed contained in $K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $A$-algebra structures on $K$ and $K'$ compatible with $L$; let $\kappa$ denote the residue field of $A$. Let $j \in K$ and $j' \in K'$ be non-zero elements both mapping to the Laurent series $q^{-1}\,j_{\mathrm{num}}$ with rational coefficients pushed into $L((q))$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is, a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series whose complex reduction is its $q$-expansion and whose image in $\kappa((q))$ is non-zero. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose members are exactly those $f$ admitting a Gauss presentation, i.e. $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K'$ consisting of the elements whose images in $K$ lie in $W_0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of ring homomorphisms $e$ from the residue field of $W_0$ and $e'$ from the residue field of $W_0'$ to $\kappa((q))$ such that: both are injective; the range of $e$ is the Igusa field $\mathrm{Ig}_\kappa(M;w)$, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by $\kappa(X_1(M))$ together with the inverse of the reduction of the $q$-expansion series of $w$; the range of $e'$ is $\kappa(X_1(M))$, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the ratios of integral forms of level $\Gamma_1(M)$; $e$ and $e'$ agree on residues of elements of $W_0'$ via the inclusion $W_0' \to W_0$; and both read off Gauss presentations, in the sense that whenever $f \cdot y = x$ with $x, y \in A[[q]]$ and $\bar y \neq 0$ one has $e(\bar f) = \bar x / \bar y$ in $\kappa((q))$ (likewise for $e'$), while for $a \in A$ with $a \in W_0$ (resp. $a \in W_0'$) the value is the constant Laurent series attached to the residue of $a$.
--
--   This identifies, inside $\kappa((q))$, the residue field extension of the Gauss valuation ring of the level-$Mp$ $q$-expansion field over that of the level-$M$ one with the extension of the Igusa function field $\mathrm{Ig}_\kappa(M;w)$ over $\kappa(X_1(M))$, compatibly with Gauss presentations and with constants from $A$. It serves as the input for the separability and unramifiedness statements at the Gauss prime used in the study of the integral models of $X_1(Mp)$ over $X_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_ringHom_residueField_eq_of_gaussPresentation_x1_mul.lean

